{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_193fbf7ee05d51232b0aa73ef4d749ce092feb37ad3d0b1a26427f4b9b9f3632","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7c3ff1e2c38b5d314f9e551a5f9c3ff954242d4e4dc437cd880711475d58a7aa"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"The product is described as a policy engine, EDR, and signed audit chain in one binary, treating AI agent tool calls in the same event taxonomy as kernel-level file, process, network, dylib, and persistence events.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_26ed14ccac4508a679ab965259c4f4e5dfca63d846fe88f5590b1179dca94bd4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1083ff5316f811a6a2d1ae401bf31a09fd3323229c4c8500b1e67d8e1604cf57"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"The engine ships in multiple forms: a Rust crate, TypeScript SDK, Python package, Go module, CLI, desktop EDR agent (macOS Endpoint Security/Network Extension; Linux Tetragon/Hubble), and an enterprise control plane.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d9a824d8b4980770542ddc8baf525956dc12717e7c1578e515fa305fda71380","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d534611a1e2acd5b5e0bf3c4e6f36468d169ba1fb1eae9ab82b5563c6b4a75c","slc_177e40a989f847d2d90e5106e7ce068a7d6bde6f6069ff9b08614bfe0955f6c8","slc_1e92e5cfd76fd77a3f7729f9af04083788d02c00dffbf38bed16f024d2ab9d59","slc_2a53ca3c77e9d4715cc897c404b84e351c792df9f4ee04f55e12329e980c0198","slc_3939783b4145abf259d03e6e9364797e5445ed2d1dd5f55a0b425d6de74f48be","slc_ae379e9bb0610a5e787b66c318318fd1eede069bce90a13bf6d5aa173abac6bd","slc_bee4d07336e80158f31bed8b8c66b0e677aad6a37f7a0ae8b4c57685e02bb08b","slc_dc5ff132705f2a141e430b72f91dfc93217cf8ba230ba99068c98795419bd82c"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"The CLI supports commands such as init --keygen, daemon start/status, check with --action-type and --ruleset, verify --policy, run --policy, and policy synth/simulate/diff subcommands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4392c4644d8683d5d0350bdd0585546465ee72cc562a65966b19cd4a403242fe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_db14a9dfa05c224c57741e15156b2bad22a3c33698bd32a7b1946e89f4f97d7e","slc_f1b0b6b1a49454d3e1d8381823d16ad189e54fbd269bbd63e98c5f419c0f6aa0","slc_fd2e2401895c029b3bd3c7fc00976d85b1afe5f50b827ed84504d40f64a3053f"],"source_ids":["src_62e022182ee4512aa8fd71aa1c147e31","src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"The system depends on Ed25519 signing (ed25519-dalek for Rust primitives), RFC 8785 JSON canonicalization for cross-language signature verification, and NATS JetStream for telemetry transport.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_67b0d569ec11835e904c8774f7a3d2666dca18575c1f2edf4705718353cca01f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_da1e05c364f1c80edf606bc3deac54a0d38cef90283c4dc29502829f7bacd4b3"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"Policies are versioned deterministic policy-as-code (schema 1.5.0, backward-compatible with 1.1.0+) supporting extends from built-ins, local files, and remote URLs that are host-allowlisted and sha256 integrity-pinned.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_983d56618f10d67da132177d25248de32e249b4fc035066041848f5dde2d16a6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_22b6edb63aa2ce519c1ad0a06e549f0ba256b764e2b813b890e167a0ce2043c4"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"Enterprise deployments use a control plane with Control API, NATS JetStream transport, Spine audit chain, and Control Console; enrollment is over mTLS with posture commands using request/reply acks and signed completion bundles.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a190c4ae9401c60564a74e5342fc9699679ee794cac646d1159c73a029a00486","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7c1f9dd4c808751431bd1bab2950dc2aa40e81a2a02105f58b523e12b6ce750d"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"Past observations are kept on a disk-backed flight recorder so a tightened policy can be simulated against prior state before deployment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a36f56bdd137e004d038c255e4d613a0127d0581309e73c96cac012dbab50f96","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_421418ad7570467813e5873de331902a9750dc3d1d222e22f2bdc436b15e4442","slc_e0a6827dcece1edc389747469b7c4b31e850b3372e90ce735982d1f3c01a712b"],"source_ids":["src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"A documented guard stack includes ForbiddenPathGuard, EgressAllowlistGuard, SecretLeakGuard, ShellCommandGuard, McpToolGuard, PromptInjectionGuard, JailbreakGuard, ComputerUseGuard, and SpiderSenseGuard, each returning a verdict with evidence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f04c576ef81938f8218e1f4cb0f176c3d697e099fa34e111e96f767af570d276","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"backbay-labs/clawdstrike@b01f63ae64fa snapshot e30732e863637655","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_433a56c8a6bec14f309a4b3b40c2815ca3a7c411daa7f72afceef6fe9d276a3c","slc_602855d31318e384c227f87f7151185e1b40bfa8002cb33294ce83e92d6c26e3","slc_7c3ff1e2c38b5d314f9e551a5f9c3ff954242d4e4dc437cd880711475d58a7aa"],"source_ids":["src_62e022182ee4512aa8fd71aa1c147e31","src_7904ef33d485509399d778d8e838d94e"],"text":"Defaults fail closed: the guard report aggregates per-guard results such that any deny produces an overall deny, and denials emit signed receipts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:37:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5b959a84a93e4cef999e5f1054b5b916"}
